# Declarative Tooltip and Pointer-Target System

Status: planned

## Goal

Replace SoulSearch's parent-aggregated tooltip lookup with a declarative widget attribute and a generic, per-screen pointer-target dispatcher. Each control owns its current tooltip text; the tooltip presentation layer reads that text from the one control selected by normal pointer targeting.

## Locked architectural decisions

- `tooltip` is a mutable text attribute on any `widgets.Widget` descendant. It is not a callback or getter.
- Controls may update `self.tooltip` whenever their state, hovered row, or backing data changes.
- The tooltip agent reads the current attribute on every update and must not retain a stale cached copy.
- Tooltip lookup stops at the selected pointer target. It never falls back to a parent widget's tooltip.
- Layout containers and parent panels are transparent to pointer targeting by default.
- A panel can explicitly opt into being a pointer target when the panel itself owns an interaction or tooltip.
- Open modal surfaces are opaque pointer barriers even when no child under the pointer has a tooltip. Controls behind them cannot become pointer targets.
- Pointer targeting is generic UI infrastructure shared with tooltip behavior; the tooltip system does not independently reverse-walk the widget hierarchy.
- Pointer state and tooltip presentation are owned per screen/window context, not by a process-global registry.
- Existing tooltip text, wrapping, placement, and immediate hover behavior remain characterization behavior during this migration.

## Non-goals

- Do not add tooltip-text getter functions, provider callbacks, or parent-level tooltip aggregators.
- Do not implement HTML-style ancestor tooltip inheritance.
- Do not combine this migration with the separate tooltip frame/branding visual cleanup in `project.todo`.
- Do not add delayed display, focus-triggered display, or Escape dismissal unless they are approved as a separate UX change.
- Do not replace semantic description modules such as `attribute_descriptions`; controls should continue using them when updating their own tooltip text.

## Phase 0 - Characterize the current behavior and freeze the contract

- [ ] Inventory every tooltip producer, forwarding method, and renderer host in the main SoulSearch screen, stats popover, and stats overlay.
- [ ] Record which tooltips are static and which depend on a row, column, picker selection, filter action, or subject record.
- [ ] Add or retain characterization tests for current tooltip text, wrapping, placement, and immediate display behavior.
- [ ] Add a characterization test proving that an open picker prevents the underlying filter-management controls from producing tooltips.
- [ ] Add a characterization test for overlapping sibling controls so the visually/input-topmost eligible control wins.
- [ ] Add a characterization test proving that a target without tooltip text produces no tooltip instead of consulting a parent.
- [ ] Add a characterization test proving that hidden controls and controls beneath hidden ancestors cannot become targets.
- [ ] Record the baseline unit-test count and package/build validation commands in this document before implementation begins.

### Phase 0 exit criteria

- [ ] Current tooltip behavior and the new targeting rules are represented by tests before production routing changes begin.

## Phase 1 - Add the common declarative widget attribute

- [ ] Audit the active DFHack widget API for an existing `tooltip` attribute or naming collision.
- [ ] Add one idempotent SoulSearch widget-extension module that declares `tooltip=DEFAULT_NIL` on the common `widgets.Widget.ATTRS` base before SoulSearch widgets are constructed.
- [ ] Verify that native widget classes such as `HotkeyLabel`, `CycleHotkeyLabel`, `Label`, and `List` accept `tooltip='text'` in their normal constructors without custom subclasses.
- [ ] Define the attribute contract: a string is current tooltip text; `nil` or an empty string means no tooltip; functions and other value types are invalid.
- [ ] Add validation or a clear failure for unsupported tooltip value types instead of silently invoking them.
- [ ] Verify that assigning `widget.tooltip` after construction updates the value observed on the next tooltip update.
- [ ] Ensure repeated module loads/reloads do not replace DFHack classes, duplicate attributes, or retain stale widget-extension state.
- [ ] Update the test environment and widget harness to model the same inherited `tooltip` attribute behavior.
- [ ] Add focused tests for constructor assignment, direct runtime mutation, clearing, and reload idempotence.

### Phase 1 exit criteria

- [ ] Any DFHack widget descendant can declare or update tooltip text without a tooltip-specific subclass or getter.

## Phase 2 - Introduce generic per-screen pointer targeting

- [ ] Create a `PointerContext`/`PointerDispatcher` abstraction whose result contains the selected widget and pointer coordinates local to that widget.
- [ ] Define an explicit targeting protocol for terminal targets, transparent containers, misses, and opaque blockers.
- [ ] Make static widgets with non-empty tooltip text eligible pointer targets without additional subclasses.
- [ ] Provide an explicit opt-in for dynamic controls that need pointer enter/move events before they have populated `tooltip`.
- [ ] Keep ordinary layout panels transparent unless they explicitly opt into targeting.
- [ ] Resolve overlapping siblings according to the same ordering used by DFHack rendering and input routing.
- [ ] Respect evaluated `visible` and `active` state across the complete ancestor chain.
- [ ] Respect frame clipping so a widget cannot be targeted outside its visible clipped bounds.
- [ ] Emit target transition events for pointer enter, pointer move, and pointer leave with local coordinates.
- [ ] Clear or replace the current target safely when it closes, becomes hidden, moves, or is removed.
- [ ] Make each open `ModalPanelWindow` an opaque pointer barrier while preserving targeting of its visible descendants.
- [ ] Ensure an empty area inside an open modal returns a blocked/no-target result instead of exposing a widget behind the modal.
- [ ] Add focused dispatcher tests for nested controls, transparent panels, explicit panel targets, sibling overlap, clipping, visibility, target removal, and modal blocking.

### Phase 2 exit criteria

- [ ] Each screen can identify exactly one current pointer target, or an explicit no-target/blocked result, without tooltip-specific hierarchy traversal.

## Phase 3 - Make tooltip presentation consume pointer state

- [ ] Separate the existing tooltip renderer from tooltip discovery and component-specific content lookup.
- [ ] Add one tooltip agent/host per screen context that observes its `PointerContext`.
- [ ] Have the agent read only `pointer_context.target.tooltip` after pointer transition handling has completed.
- [ ] Read the attribute on every update so direct control mutations are visible without callbacks or change subscriptions.
- [ ] Hide the tooltip immediately when there is no target, the target is blocked, or the current attribute is `nil`/empty.
- [ ] Preserve the existing tooltip wrapping, screen-edge positioning, pens, and immediate hover timing.
- [ ] Render the tooltip above ordinary screen content without allowing it to become the underlying control's pointer target.
- [ ] Ensure tooltip rendering cannot leak pointer state or text between separate SoulSearch windows, popovers, or overlay instances.
- [ ] Add focused tests for live text mutation, clearing text while hovered, target changes, modal blocking, and per-screen isolation.

### Phase 3 exit criteria

- [ ] Tooltip presentation depends only on the screen's current pointer target and that target's current `tooltip` attribute.

## Phase 4 - Migrate static tooltip declarations

- [ ] Move static main-window and filter-management button tooltips directly onto their native widget declarations.
- [ ] Move results-column header tooltips directly onto the corresponding native `CycleHotkeyLabel` widgets.
- [ ] Move stats-column header tooltips directly onto the corresponding header widgets.
- [ ] Move picker buttons, close buttons, scope controls, and preset controls with static text to their own `tooltip` attributes.
- [ ] Remove `FILTER_CONTROL_TOOLTIPS` and other centralized view-id-to-text tables once all entries are declared by their controls.
- [ ] Remove static tooltip hit-test helpers that exist only to support parent aggregation.
- [ ] Update component tests to assert the widgets' declared attributes rather than calling parent tooltip lookup methods.

### Phase 4 exit criteria

- [ ] Every static tooltip is declared next to the control it describes, with no parent-maintained tooltip table.

## Phase 5 - Migrate dynamic tooltip ownership

- [ ] Update `FilterActionList` to derive and assign its own `tooltip` during pointer enter/move and clear it when no action owns the local position.
- [ ] Update searchable picker/list controls to assign descriptor tooltip text for their own hovered choices.
- [ ] Keep attribute, skill, preset, race, and unit-scope description lookup inside the control that owns the displayed choice.
- [ ] Update `UnitStatsList` to assign header, stat, delta, and row-description tooltip text from local pointer coordinates and its current subject records.
- [ ] Ensure dynamic controls refresh `tooltip` when backing data changes while the pointer remains over the same target.
- [ ] Ensure blank rows, separators, padding, and non-descriptive regions explicitly clear dynamic tooltip text.
- [ ] Remove tooltip forwarding methods from `StatsPanel`, picker parents, and other composite controls after their children own the text.
- [ ] Add focused component tests for coordinate-to-text mapping and direct attribute updates without involving the tooltip renderer.

### Phase 5 exit criteria

- [ ] Dynamic controls own and maintain their current tooltip text; no ancestor computes tooltip content on their behalf.

## Phase 6 - Remove legacy aggregation and wire every host

- [ ] Wire `SoulSearchScreen` to construct and update one pointer context and tooltip agent for its widget tree.
- [ ] Wire the stats popover and stats overlay to their own isolated pointer contexts and tooltip agents.
- [ ] Remove `SoulSearchWindow:get_tooltip_text()` and its hard-coded precedence chain.
- [ ] Remove `FilterPanel:get_control_tooltip()`, `get_filter_action_tooltip()`, `get_descriptor_tooltip()`, and superseded button helpers.
- [ ] Remove `ResultsPanel:get_header_tooltip()`, `UnitStatsList:get_tooltip_text()`, and tooltip-only forwarding methods after their replacements are active.
- [ ] Remove `get_text` callback wiring from `SoulSearchTooltip` construction and rename the renderer/host types if their old names no longer describe their responsibilities.
- [ ] Remove duplicated visibility and mouse-over helpers that are no longer used outside legacy tooltip discovery.
- [ ] Update `module_registry.lua` load ordering for the widget extension, pointer infrastructure, and tooltip host.
- [ ] Search production code and tests for obsolete getter/provider callback APIs and parent-level tooltip precedence logic.
- [ ] Replace legacy parent-precedence tests with pointer-target and control-ownership integration tests.

### Phase 6 exit criteria

- [ ] No window or parent component aggregates descendant tooltips, and no tooltip renderer accepts a content getter callback.

## Phase 7 - Validate reloads, packaging, and live modal behavior

- [ ] Run the focused pointer, modal-panel, filter-panel, results-panel, stats-panel, popover, overlay, and tooltip tests.
- [ ] Run the complete test suite with `tools/Test.ps1` and record the final passing count.
- [ ] Run `tools/Build.ps1` and `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1`.
- [ ] Reload SoulSearch repeatedly in a live DFHack session and verify the common widget attribute remains available without duplicate-class or stale-module failures.
- [ ] Verify static tooltips on native widgets in the main SoulSearch window.
- [ ] Verify dynamic filter-action, picker-choice, results-header, stats-header, and stats-row tooltips.
- [ ] Open every filter picker and confirm underlying filter-management tooltips never appear through the modal.
- [ ] Move the pointer across picker padding and blank rows and confirm stale tooltip text is cleared.
- [ ] Open multiple SoulSearch windows and confirm pointer targets and tooltip text remain isolated per window.
- [ ] Verify the stats popover and overlay use the same declarative behavior without sharing state with the main screen.
- [ ] Update this plan, relevant architecture documentation, and the `project.todo` tracking entry with final completion status.

### Phase 7 exit criteria

- [ ] Unit tests, build/package validation, reload checks, and live modal/input scenarios all pass.

## Final acceptance criteria

- [ ] Any native or SoulSearch widget can declare `tooltip='text'` without a custom tooltip subclass.
- [ ] Controls can dynamically replace or clear their tooltip attribute and the visible tooltip reflects the new value on the next update.
- [ ] Tooltip content is never supplied through a getter/provider callback.
- [ ] Tooltip lookup never falls back to a parent.
- [ ] Parent/layout containers are transparent unless explicitly targetable.
- [ ] Open modal panels prevent all underlying controls from becoming pointer targets within the modal's blocked region.
- [ ] Tooltip resolution, text, and visibility state are isolated per screen instance.
- [ ] No parent window contains a descendant-tooltip map or precedence chain.
